arguments.prompt:
You are building a Blazor Web App for a university course catalog. The project is at `/tmp/sv-06857ae25a244b3e90a1faffff8fb06a/UniversityCourseCatalog`. It was created with `dotnet new blazor -int None` (Static SSR only).

CRITICAL: No `@rendermode`, no `@onclick`, no JS interop. Forms use POST with `[SupplyParameterFromForm]` and `<AntiforgeryToken />`. Search/filter uses GET form with `[SupplyParameterFromQuery]`.

Please create/modify all the files below. After creating everything, run `dotnet build` to verify it compiles.

## 1. Create Models

**Models/Department.cs**:
```csharp
namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class Department
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

**Models/Instructor.cs**:
```csharp
namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class Instructor
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Bio { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Email { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public int DepartmentId { get; set; }
}
```

**Models/Course.cs**:
```csharp
namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class Course
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public int Credits { get; set; }
    public string Schedule { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public int DepartmentId { get; set; }
    public int InstructorId { get; set; }
    public bool IsFeatured { get; set; }
}
```

**Models/EnrollmentRequest.cs**:
```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class EnrollmentRequest
{
    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Student Name is required.")]
    public string StudentName { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Student ID is required.")]
    public string StudentId { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    [Range(1, int.MaxValue, ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    public int CourseId { get; set; }

    public DateTime SubmittedAt { get; set; }
}
```

## 2. Create Services/CatalogService.cs

Create a comprehensive in-memory service with:
- 4 departments: Computer Science (CS), Mathematics (MATH), English (ENG), Physics (PHYS)
- 1 instructor per department (4 total)
- 3 courses per department (12 total), some marked IsFeatured
- Methods: GetDepartments(), GetCourses(), GetCourseById(int id), GetCoursesByDepartment(int departmentId), SearchCourses(string? search, int? departmentId), GetDepartmentById(int id), GetInstructorById(int id), GetFeaturedCourses(), SubmitEnrollment(EnrollmentRequest request)

Make realistic course names, schedules, descriptions.

## 3. Update Program.cs

Add `using UniversityCourseCatalog.Services;` and register `builder.Services.AddSingleton<CatalogService>();` before `var app = builder.Build();`.

## 4. Replace Components/Pages/Home.razor

```razor
@page "/"
@using UniversityCourseCatalog.Services
@inject CatalogService CatalogService

<PageTitle>University Course Catalog</PageTitle>

<div class="hero-section">
    <h1>Welcome to the University Course Catalog</h1>
    <p>Explore our departments, browse courses, and enroll today.</p>
    <a href="/courses" class="btn-primary-link">Browse All Courses</a>
</div>

<section class="featured-section">
    <h2>Featured Courses</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
        @foreach (var course in CatalogService.GetFeaturedCourses())
        {
            <div class="card">
                <h3><a href="/courses/@course.Id">@course.Code</a></h3>
                <p class="card-title">@course.Title</p>
                <p class="card-meta">@course.Credits Credits &bull; @course.Schedule</p>
            </div>
        }
    </div>
</section>

<section class="departments-section">
    <h2>Departments</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
        @foreach (var dept in CatalogService.GetDepartments())
        {
            <div class="card">
                <h3><a href="/courses?DepartmentId=@dept.Id">@dept.Name</a></h3>
                <p>@dept.Description</p>
            </div>
        }
    </div>
</section>
```

## 5. Create Components/Pages/Courses.razor

```razor
@page "/courses"
@using UniversityCourseCatalog.Services
@inject CatalogService CatalogService

<PageTitle>Courses - University Course Catalog</PageTitle>

<h1>Course Catalog</h1>

<form method="get" class="search-form">
    <div class="search-controls">
        <input type="text" name="Search" value="@Search" placeholder="Search courses..." class="form-input" />
        <select name="DepartmentId" class="form-select">
            <option value="">All Departments</option>
            @foreach (var dept in CatalogService.GetDepartments())
            {
                <option value="@dept.Id" selected="@(DepartmentId == dept.Id)">@dept.Name</option>
            }
        </select>
        <button type="submit" class="btn-primary">Search</button>
    </div>
</form>

@{
    var courses = CatalogService.SearchCourses(Search, DepartmentId);
}

@if (!courses.Any())
{
    <p class="no-results">No courses found.</p>
}
else
{
    <table class="course-table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Code</th>
                <th>Title</th>
                <th>Credits</th>
                <th>Schedule</th>
                <th></th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var course in courses)
            {
                <tr>
                    <td>@course.Code</td>
                    <td><a href="/courses/@course.Id">@course.Title</a></td>
                    <td>@course.Credits</td>
                    <td>@course.Schedule</td>
                    <td><a href="/courses/@course.Id">Details</a></td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
}

@code {
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery]
    public string? Search { get; set; }

    [SupplyParameterFromQuery]
    public int? DepartmentId { get; set; }
}
```

## 6. Create Components/Pages/CourseDetail.razor

```razor
@page "/courses/{Id:int}"
@using UniversityCourseCatalog.Services
@inject CatalogService CatalogService

@{
    var course = CatalogService.GetCourseById(Id);
}

@if (course is null)
{
    <PageTitle>Course Not Found</PageTitle>
